# Wave W17-V (Route 206): stray post — a cave-mouth marker post flanking the Stray Cave mouths under the pillars: a plain post carrying one black cave band, the dark mouth’s own mark cut into the wood (design: the cave under the cycling road, dark and echoing; the sign names it, the posts flank its doors). On pillar turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from Route 204’s red-banded scree post by the black band: the scree post warns of falling stone, the stray post only says the dark is here.
